      },
      "option_expiry_impact": 4,
      "option_expiry_importance": {"daily": 20, "weekly": 35, "monthly": 50, "quarterly": 60},
      "note_option_expiry_importance": "Importance (0-100) of a Deribit options expiry by tenor, written to the calendar row as importance_score (the event layer reads a row's importance_score before the class value): quarterly = the last Friday of March, June, September or December, monthly = the last Friday of any other month, weekly = any other Friday, daily = every other day. A routine daily expiry (no size information, impact 4/10) scores 0.30 x 20 + 0.20 x 40 + 15 + 1.25 + 5 = 35.3 at its closest, below the 40 a 'next key event' needs, so it no longer displaces the week's real events every morning; the quarterly expiry (60) can.",
      "fomc_impact": 10,
      "earnings_impact": 6,
      "legislation_impact": 5,
      "fetch_days": 45,
      "fomc_press_conference_time": "14:30",
      "fomc_press_conference_impact": 9,
      "fomc_attribution": "Source: Federal Reserve Board",
      "fomc_time_basis": "FOMC statement 2:00 p.m. ET (configured standard time; fomccalendars.htm lists dates only; federalreserve.gov calendar.json lists 2:00 p.m.)",
      "fomc_press_conference_time_basis": "Chair's press conference 2:30 p.m. ET (configured; federalreserve.gov calendar.json lists 2:30 p.m.); sub-event of the decision",
      "note_hygiene": "A successful refresh replaces the provider's stored rows inside its fetch window (rescheduled or cancelled rows disappear; rows with an actual are kept). The same release from two providers is deduplicated by (event_class, sub_event, symbol, publisher-local date, speaker for speeches/testimony): an exact time beats a rule time beats a date, then provider_priority (official first). Values are never lost: every metric row of the release (e.g. FMP CPI MoM / YoY / core) is kept on the surviving row as metrics [{name, provider, consensus, actual, previous, unit, ...}], and the headline metric (dedupe.headline_metrics, first matching pattern; a lone metric otherwise) is lent as the row's consensus/actual with values_source, lent_fields and headline_metric. A row with a structured vendor estimate (Finnhub) keeps its estimate and is lent the actual only.",
      "decision_classes": ["FOMC", "ECB", "BOE", "BOJ"],
      "kinds": {
        "note": "Row kind (docs/EVENT_AWARENESS.md §8): an explicit kind wins, then the sub_event, then DECISION for a decision class, then the event class, then the category; unknown stays null (the event engine derives it). is_decision is true only for DECISION rows of decision_classes.",
        "values": ["DECISION", "PRESS_CONFERENCE", "MINUTES", "SPEECH", "TESTIMONY", "PROJECTIONS", "RELEASE", "AUCTION", "EARNINGS",
                   "EXPIRY", "STATEMENT", "OTHER"],
        "sub_events": ["PRESS_CONFERENCE", "MINUTES", "PROJECTIONS", "STATEMENT"],
        "classes": {"EARNINGS": "EARNINGS", "CRYPTO_EXPIRY": "EXPIRY", "FOMC_MINUTES": "MINUTES", "FED_BEIGE_BOOK": "RELEASE"},
